# VERSION

Civic Tech Field Guide Design System — token releases.

    CURRENT: 2.0.0 · 2026-08-12

Read it at runtime instead of diffing:

```js
getComputedStyle(document.documentElement).getPropertyValue('--ctfg-tokens-version') // "2.0.0"
getComputedStyle(document.documentElement).getPropertyValue('--ctfg-tokens-date')    // "2026-08-12"
```

Every file in `tokens/` carries the same v-string in its header comment. The version is **system-wide**,
not per-file: a file whose contents did not change in a release still gets the new v-string, so a
vendored set is always internally consistent. If two files in a set disagree, the set is a bad copy.

The bundle folder UUID (`ctfg-design-system-<hex>`) is a build identifier with no ordering. It is not a
version. Do not compare two of them.

## Versioning policy

- **MAJOR** — a token's *rendered value* changes, or an alias is repointed at a different value, or a
  token is renamed or removed. Anything a consumer might see or have overridden. Check your override
  layer on a major.
- **MINOR** — new tokens added; comments, documentation, or role guidance clarified. Existing values
  untouched.
- **PATCH** — no token-layer change; component or docs fixes only.

Repointing an alias is deliberately MAJOR even though no hex literal in the file moved, because the
rendered output changes for every consumer. That is exactly the class of change that shipped silently
in 2.0.0's predecessor and caused the defect it fixes.

## Vendorable set

These four files are the supported vendorable set. An update reaches a vendoring consumer by replacing
them:

    tokens/colors.css
    tokens/typography.css
    tokens/spacing.css
    tokens/effects.css

Deliberately **not** in the vendorable set:

| file | why not |
|---|---|
| `styles.css` | contains no rules; its only non-`@import` line loads Google Fonts |
| `tokens/fonts.css` | `@font-face` against a CDN — same data-residency objection |
| `tokens/interactions.css` | rules keyed to `.ctfg-*` classes, not tokens |
| `_ds_bundle.js` | React components |

Consumers with their own component CSS should take the interaction and component layers as **intent +
values** from the release notes, not as files.

## Sanctioned divergences

Consumers may hold these permanently. They are not drift and should survive every update:

- **Self-hosted webfonts, no font CDN.** Skipping `styles.css` and `tokens/fonts.css` and declaring the
  same families from same-origin `woff2` is expected behaviour for consumers serving EU public-sector
  readers, where a `fonts.googleapis.com` request is a live GDPR objection. Font *stacks* with fuller
  fallbacks, and dropping `Cascadia Code` from `--font-mono`, are part of this divergence.
  The system side is arguably the one that should change here.

