## 2.0.0 · 2026-08-12 — accessibility: text and green token semantics

WCAG 2.1 AA. **No new colour values** — every fix repoints an alias at a value already in the palette.
Full detail: `handoff-accessibility-2026-08-12.md`. For a consumer with its own component CSS:
`handoff-govoss-catalog.md`.

**Token layer (`colors.css`) — this is what a vendoring consumer gets:**

| token | 1.0.0 | 2.0.0 |
|---|---|---|
| `--ink-soft` | `#6B6B68` (ink-500) | **`#4D4D4A`** (ink-600) |
| `--ink-faint` | `#9FA4A3` (ink-400) | **`#6B6B68`** (ink-500) |
| `--ink-400` | `#9FA4A3` | `#9FA4A3` — unchanged, role narrowed to **non-text only** |
| `--green-text` | — | **`#006348`** (new) |
| `--on-green` | — | **`#19191E`** (new) |
| `--green-line` | — | **`#006348`** (new) |
| `--green`, `--verified` | `#01B583` | `#01B583` — unchanged, **fill only** |

**If you carry a local patch for `--ink-faint`, 2.0.0 is where you delete it.** The fix is in the token
file now; a patch on top is a no-op that will read as a divergence to the next person.

**`--ink-soft` is a required companion change, and it is visually unreviewed.** With `--ink-faint` on
ink-500, leaving `--ink-soft` there too makes secondary and tertiary text the identical colour — the
accessibility fix deletes a tier of the hierarchy. The rebalance restores three steps (17.4:1 / 8.5:1 /
5.35:1 on white) but darkens *every* secondary string in the system, and no one has reviewed that in a
real page. Look at it before shipping; see `handoff-govoss-catalog.md` §4.1 for the alternative.

**Interaction layer (`interactions.css`) — intent, for consumers who don't take the file:** `#01B583`
is a *light* fill and takes ink; `#006348` is a *dark* fill and takes white. Any state that swaps one
fill for the other must swap the label with it — the secondary button's hover darkens to `#006348` and
so moves its label from `#19191E` to `#FFFFFF` (ink on `#006348` is 2.40:1).

**Component layer — intent:** endorsement stamp keeps the `#01B583` fill and `--shadow-green`, moving
only its label and seal (`#006348` on the soft variant, `#19191E` on the filled one). Green borders take
`--green-line`. Icons ship `aria-hidden="true"` + `focusable="false"`, with `aria-label` opting into
`role="img"` for a glyph that carries meaning alone.

